   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Hello Cheryl</div><div>It&#39;s possible you&#39;ve hit on a blind spot in my coding of modelAverage (a condition I didn&#39;t allow for, and that I should fix), but there&#39;s some teasing out before I go there.</div><div><br></div><div>The result from modelAverage is &quot;an array of model-averaged estimates&quot; - you shouldn&#39;t expect predict to work on that. <br></div><div><br></div><div>Your problem seems to be that &#39;avg&#39; doesn&#39;t include all levels of &quot;Treatment&quot;. &#39;newdata&#39; is the way to get that, but I don&#39;t see what you have attempted there.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Pushing back on a couple of points. Would you really expect the learned response to differ between treatments (i.e. why not b + Treatment)? Spacing your code would make it more readable.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Murray<br></div>"
    ],
